  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class=3D"wrap">
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">04</span><h2>Te=
st run lifecycle</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-intro">What happens for one test method, from suite=
 start to the cross-run summary.</p>
    <ol class=3D"steps">
      <li><strong>Maven Surefire</strong> loads <code>src/test/resources/su=
ites/testng.xml</code> (overridable with <code>-Dsuite.xml</code>) and regi=
sters <code>TestListener</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>BaseTest @BeforeMethod</strong> calls <code>BROWSER_SESSI=
ON.FIRST.start()</code>, which acquires a permit, creates the driver for th=
e configured browser/headless mode, and stores it in this thread's map.</li>
      <li><strong>Test class @BeforeMethod</strong> sets up state through s=
ervices, e.g. <code>loginService.loginAsStandardUser()</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>@Test</strong> chains service calls. Services create page=
s/modules per call, read values and pass them to <code>*Assertions</code>.<=
/li>
      <li><strong>TestListener</strong> logs PASS/FAIL/SKIP, captures <code=
>target/screenshots/&lt;test&gt;_&lt;ts&gt;.png</code> on failure, and reco=
rds the scenario outcome (method + data-provider params) in <code>FlakyTest=
Detector</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>BaseTest @AfterMethod</strong> stops every session still =
open on the thread, releasing each permit, even if the test forgot to.</li>
      <li><strong>Suite finish</strong>: the listener compares this run wit=
h the last 10 in <code>RunHistoryStore</code>, logs <code>[FLAKY]</code> sc=
enarios, writes <code>target/test-result-summary.json</code>, and persists =
this run.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class=3D"wrap">
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">05</span><h2>Te=
st intelligence: flaky detection &amp; impact analysis</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-intro">Two browser-free utilities turn run results =
and a committed dependency graph into actionable reports. They share one co=
mparator/analyzer between the live listener and an on-demand picocli CLI.</=
p>
    <div class=3D"layer-grid">
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t2">Flakiness</span>
        <h3>FlakyTestDetector + RunHistoryStore</h3>
        <p>A scenario is flaky if it both passed and failed across the curr=
ent run and stored history. A scenario with no history is never flagged.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>History: <code>src/test/resources/data/previousTestResults/ru=
n-*.json</code>, last 10 kept</li>
          <li>Override with <code>-DrunHistoryStore.directory</code></li>
          <li>Output: <code>target/test-result-summary.json</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t2">Selection</span>
        <h3>TestImpactAnalyzer</h3>
        <p>Maps changed functional areas to the test classes that cover the=
m, from <code>testimpact/dependency-graph.json</code>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Areas: <code>driver</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>login<=
/code>, <code>inventory</code>, <code>cart</code>, <code>checkout</code></l=
i>
          <li>New test class =E2=86=92 register in the suite and the graph<=
/li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t2">CLI</span>
        <h3>CliMain (picocli)</h3>
        <p><code>flaky-report</code> and <code>impact-analysis</code> print=
 results and write HTML to <code>target/cli-reports/</code>. They never run=
 tests or open a browser.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>CliHtmlReportWriter</code> renders the report</li>
          <li>Wrapper scripts in <code>src/main/resources/scripts/</code></=
li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
<pre class=3D"cmd"><span class=3D"c"># which classes does a cart change aff=
ect?</span>
mvn -q compile exec:java -Dexec.args=3D"impact-analysis --changed-area=3Dca=
rt"
<span class=3D"c"># which scenarios flip between pass and fail across store=
d runs?</span>
mvn -q compile exec:java -Dexec.args=3D"flaky-report"</pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class=3D"wrap">
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">06</span><h2>Wh=
at each layer owns</h2></div>
    <div class=3D"layer-grid">
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Tests</span>
        <h3>*Test extends BaseTest</h3>
        <p>Business-readable flows. Setup in <code>@BeforeMethod</code>, pa=
rametrization via <code>@DataProvider</code>.</p>
        <ul><li>Only service calls</li><li>No locators, <code>Assert</code>=
 or driver</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Services</span>
        <h3>*Service</h3>
        <p>One per functional area. Orchestrate pages/modules, pass read va=
lues to assertions, return <code>this</code>.</p>
        <ul><li>Create pages per call =E2=86=92 always the current thread's=
 driver</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Pages</span>
        <h3>BasePage / LoggedInPage</h3>
        <p>One class per screen: <code>By</code> locators plus interactions=
 that return raw values or the next page.</p>
        <ul><li>Wait-wrapped <code>click</code>/<code>type</code>/<code>get=
Text</code></li><li>Never assert</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t2">Page modules</span>
        <h3>pages/modules/*Module</h3>
        <p>Shared UI fragments, reached from pages via accessors (<code>hea=
der()</code>, <code>errorMessage()</code>).</p>
        <ul><li>HeaderModule =C2=B7 BurgerMenuModule =C2=B7 ErrorMessageMod=
ule</li><li>Locators for a fragment live once</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag">Assertions</span>
        <h3>*Assertions</h3>
        <p>Value-in verifications with meaningful TestNG <code>Assert</code=
> messages.</p>
        <ul><li>Never touch pages or the driver</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t3">Driver</span>
        <h3>DriverManager =C2=B7 BrowserSession =C2=B7 DriverFactory</h3>
        <p>ThreadLocal session map, permit-guarded start/stop, per-browser =
options via Selenium Manager.</p>
        <ul><li>Chrome / Firefox / Edge, headless-aware</li><li><code>MAX_B=
ROWSER_SESSIONS</code> cap</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t3">Config &amp; waits</span>
        <h3>ConfigReader =C2=B7 TestData =C2=B7 WaitUtils</h3>
        <p><code>config.properties</code>, where any key can be overridden =
with <code>-D</code>. FluentWait-based explicit waits, with implicit wait k=
ept at 0.</p>
        <ul><li><code>waitForStablePosition</code> guards CSS transitions</=
li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"layer-card">
        <span class=3D"tag t3">Diagnostics</span>
        <h3>TestListener =C2=B7 ScreenshotUtils</h3>
        <p>Screenshot on failure for the failing thread's driver, SLF4J log=
ging, and flaky-outcome recording.</p>
        <ul><li>Skips the screenshot when no browser is active (unit tests)=
</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

