<section>
  <div class=3D"wrap">
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">08</span><h2>Ke=
y decisions</h2></div>
    <div class=3D"table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Tests =E2=86=92 services only</td><td =
class=3D"why">Tests stay business-readable and immune to locator churn. Pag=
es and assertions can be refactored without touching a single test.</td></t=
r>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Reusable page modules</td><td class=3D=
"why">Header, menu and error-banner markup repeats across screens. Modellin=
g each once removes duplicated locators, and a UI change to a shared fragme=
nt becomes a one-file fix.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Assertions as a separate layer</td><td=
 class=3D"why">Verifications take plain values, so they're reusable across =
flows and never hide extra UI interaction.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Session per test method, permit-capped=
</td><td class=3D"why">Isolation holds under any TestNG parallel mode. The =
semaphore bounds real browser count independently of <code>thread-count</co=
de>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Selenium Manager</td><td class=3D"why"=
>Driver binaries resolve automatically, with nothing browser-version-specif=
ic checked in.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Explicit waits only</td><td class=3D"w=
hy">Implicit wait stays 0. <code>WaitUtils</code> is the single source of p=
olling, including stable-position waits for animated elements.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Config file + <code>-D</code> override=
</td><td class=3D"why">Local defaults in one file. CI flips <code>browser</=
code>, <code>headless</code>, <code>thread.count</code> or <code>base.url</=
code> without code changes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Cross-run flaky detection</td><td clas=
s=3D"why">A single run can't tell flaky from broken. Keying outcomes by met=
hod + parameters over the last 10 runs can.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class=3D"decision">Committed impact graph</td><td class=
=3D"why">A UI suite is slow, so changes can run only the classes covering t=
he touched areas.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

